      <p>
        <strong>2017-2024 (America First?)</strong>: Military spending rose to $700-900 billion. Deaths from American military action: approximately 15,000-25,000 direct, 100,000+ enabled (Yemen, Ukraine, Gaza). My taxpayer contribution: approximately $50,000-60,000.
      </p>

      <h3>The Totals</h3>

      <p>
        Summing across fifty years:
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Total US military spending (1975-2024)</strong>: Approximately $25-30 trillion (2024 dollars)
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Total deaths attributable to American military action</strong>: Approximately 500,000-1,000,000 direct; 2,000,000-4,000,000 including enabled and indirect deaths
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>My lifetime military tax contribution</strong>: Approximately $160,000-200,000
